Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC32)
Research: Q1 (HEAD /api/hello comes with User-Agent Bun/... and no X-App, so it stays unknown)
Why this approach: a value type with Name and Match reading only two headers; the core.Profile conformance check sits in the external test package so profile.go never imports core.
Alternatives rejected: case-insensitive or substring matching on User-Agent (the spec says "starts with"); matching any x-app value (the spec names x-app: cli).
Trade-off / known limit: x-app must equal "cli" exactly; a client that spoofs either header is labelled claude-code, which is fine for detection-only labelling.
